docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md#L123).\n- `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` now covers the new `slice-type` guard cases: tooling success, missing field, cohort misuse, and tooling-id mismatch. See [/Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane/tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh#L706](file:///Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane/tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh#L706).\n- `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` now expects the explicit tag-absent warning from the scaffolder. See [/Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane/tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh#L169](file:///Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane/tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh#L169).\n\nValidation passed:\n- `shellcheck scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh`\n- `shellcheck scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\n- `shellcheck tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh`\n- `shellcheck tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`\n- `bash tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh`\n- `bash tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`\n- All required `grep -qE` checks from the orchestrator spec\n\nI left the pre-existing out-of-scope review-artifact changes in the worktree untouched."}}
